 William L. Meaney BSc, MEng, MSIA | President, CEO & Director | Age 65 | Compensation: $3.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 29K people. Revenue per employee of $235K ranks in the bottom quartile among Real Estate peers, improving at 5%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 15\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Iron Mountain Incorporated (Del is a large-cap real estate business with a $31.7B market cap on $6.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years and +9% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $932M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 7.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.9% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $22.1M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["16 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Real Estate sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"What Is Behind Iron Mountain (IRM) Raising Its Dividend By 15%?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/behind-iron-mountain-irm-raising-230858091.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794006538.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.599,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Does Iron Mountain (IRM) 15% Dividend Hike Change The Income Case?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/real-estate/nyse-irm/iron-mountain/news/does-iron-mountain-irm-15-dividend-hike-change-the-income-ca","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793953756.204,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.945,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Iron Mountain Inc (IRM) (Q3 2026) Earnings Call Highlights: Record Revenue, Raised Guidance and ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/st