:0.0,"weight":0.1}},"data_summaries":{"sect":["Its 17% operating margin trails the Real Estate median (23%) by 6pp, so it is a below-average operator in its field.","It earns less of the sector's profit than its revenue share would suggest (0.85x).","It accounts for 1.9% of sector revenue and 1.6% of sector operating profit.","Over five years it has been losing share of the sector profit pool (-7.5% a year).","The sector is fragmented and competitive (HHI 0.03 across 145 companies in the universe; the top four hold 25% of revenue), so pricing power is hard to come by."],"mkt":["The shares have drifted higher, up 19% over the past year excluding the latest month, though it has pulled back 13% over the last three months.","The price sits mid-way through its 52-week range, 21% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 35% and a beta of 1.03, it moves roughly with the market.","Liquidity is deep, with about $158.8M traded a day.","In past sell-offs it fell 36% in the 2020 crash, 23% in the 2022 bear market and 53% in 2008."],"val":["On multiples it looks expensive against Real Estate peers: P/E 76.1 vs 23.6 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 127% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of -2.9% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 2.3% (vs the 8% bar).","The 11 covering analysts target $144 on average, 35% above the price."],"prof":["ROIC of 7% falls short of the cost of capital of 7.9%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have been steady (CV 0.23).","It burns cash (FCF margin -13%).","AFFO margin (a proxy for distributable REIT cash) is -13%.","It spends 2.0% of revenue on stock compensation (above the 2% gate)."],"hlth":["Leverage is heavy at 7.4x net debt to EBITDA ($158.5M of cash against $16.4B of debt), and interest cover is thin at 1.4x.","Warning signs: an Altman Z of 1.33 in the distress zone, which caps the rating at HOLD.","The current ratio of 0.74 means short-term liabilities exceed current assets."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 10.6% over 3 years, 10.7% over 5 years and 8.7% over 10 years.","At current returns, reinvesting 100% of profits supports about 6.6% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Forward indicators: a backlog worth 0% of annual revenue, deferred revenue up 30% and FFO growth of 6.3% a year over five years.","Capex runs 2.2x depreciation (32.9% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth.","Its Rule of 40 score is -5, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.9%), and institutions hold 87%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (21 sales, net $22.1M sold).","It returns 2.9% a year to shareholders (3.2% in dividends).","The share count has grown 0.5% a year over five years, diluting existing holders.","It pays out 226% of earnings, more than it earns, so the dividend is at risk."],"people":["With about 29,400 employees, each generates about $235K of revenue, 0.1x the Real Estate median, and productivity has risen 5.4% a year.","Free cash flow is negative, at -$32K per employee.","CEO pay is $3.5M (15x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $5K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"INSUFFICIENT DATA","conv":null,"head":"Not enough data to value it: missing price or fair value.","pros":[],"cons":[],"flags":[],"need":[],"buy_below":null,"vc":null,"med":{"pe":23.5593,"ev_ebitda":16.316,"pfcf":17.832,"pb":1.3568,"roic":0.0411,"gross_margin":0.5765,"fcf_margin":0.1733,"div_yield":0.0479}},"ticker":"IRM","date":"2026-11-06"}